   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>essentially all inla models can be run via the inlabru interface, so it just depends on if it has been implemented as an inla() model.</div><div>I see a lognormalsurv in INLA::inla.doc(&quot;lognormalsurv&quot;) so looks like it should work.</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, 22 Jul 2026 at 17:36, &#39;Jonas&#39; via R-inla discussion group &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r-inla-disc...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"><font face=\"Sans Serif\">Hi,</font></div><div style=\"font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"><font face=\"Sans Serif\">I am currently setting up a joint model with INLABRU, where one of the likelihoods is left-censored due to a limit of detection. </font><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;\">I already looked into a </span><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;;font-size:14px;margin:0px;border-bottom:1px solid rgb(240,242,245)\">lognormal.surv</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;\"> and </span><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;;font-size:14px;margin:0px;border-bottom:1px solid rgb(240,242,245)\">loglogisticsurv</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;\">, but I need more distributional flexibility to capture the shape of my data.</span></div><div style=\"font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"><font face=\"Sans Serif\">Is it possible to use a </font><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;\">3-parameter weibull or a mixture of distributions (lognormalsurv &amp; lognormal) within INLABRU? Or other flexible options to consider?</span></div><div style=\"font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"><font face=\"Sans Serif\">Kind regards,</font></div><div style=\"font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"><font face=\"Sans Serif\">Jonas Meijerink</font></div><div style=\"font-family:&quot;Google Sans&quot;,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin:12px 0px 16px;border-bottom:0px rgb(10,10,10)\"></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
